  The library manifest AGP merges into the generated app's manifest.

  NOTHING TO DECLARE, and that is worth stating rather than leaving unexplained:
  `android.speech.tts.TextToSpeech` needs no `<uses-permission>` (it is not a
  dangerous permission, not a runtime-requested one, and not gated behind a
  foreground-service type the way `foray-audio`'s mediaPlayback service is) and
  this plugin adds no `<service>`, `<receiver>` or `<activity>` of its own --
  `TextToSpeech`'s engine binding is entirely internal to the framework class.
  An empty manifest merge is the correct, minimal one here, not an oversight.
-->
